a fire tore through the roof of the  vacant crazy horse 2 nightclub last  night it's located on industrial road  right north of sahara joe mohler shows  us what happened after flames broke out  early this morning  flames could be seen towering over this  building early this morning you can see  the mess on the outside and the damage  to the building people we talked to say  they woke up to the smell of smoke and a  sound of sirens  this is video from just after three  sunday morning dozens of fire crews  responded to the old crazy horse too  fighting it from the ground and above  smoke could be seen all the way in  henderson las vegas fire and rescue  tells us they had to take a defensive  strategy to fight it because of the size  of the flames no injuries were reported  you don't see that every day many many  emergency vehicles all around shane  ducour who lives nearby says he wondered  what was going to happen to this  well-known building it's like are they  going to do anything with that you know  it looks like a big building it looks  kind of  it stands out the now vacant gentlemen's  club had a long well-known history one  of the former owners rick rizzolo sold  the property after it was raided by the  fbi back in 2003 he pled guilty to  failing to pay payroll taxes he was  known for suspected mob ties the federal  government owned the building for some  time before it was sold the club has sat  empty for many years many wondering what  would happen to her fire crews were out  here for much of the morning putting out  hot spots investigators are still trying  to determine the cause reporting near  the strip joe muller live local now
 

